  "utmEpsg": 32616,
  "unverified": "No cenote of the map has a position in the database (the Xcaret sistema's only cave has neither name nor coordinates), and none of its cenotes or its open Xcaret airspace shows on the satellite (park buildings and canopy now). Placed only by the surface features the map copies from Andrews 1975 - the caleta de Xcaret and the coast, which match the satellite's shape well - but those are drawn about 15% larger than the cave survey's own scale (a similarity fit on them gives 0.163 m/px, the scale bar 0.1415 m/px, and the bar agrees with the survey's 'p. 111 m' and 'p. 135 m to Xcaret airspace' measured along the drawn passage: 0.142 and 0.147 m/px), so the cave's registration to them is uncertain; possibly 20-40 m off at the north end.",
  "placementWhy": "Scale bar (60 m = 424 px, 0.1415 m/px, checked against the written penetrations: cenote de los franceses to the airspace's south edge, 111 m = 780 px drawn; the north end to the airspace, 135 m = 921 px) and the north arrow (13.6 deg left of up; the caleta's own fit says 17 deg), shifted onto three points of the caleta and coast (surface features after Andrews 1975): the caleta channel's north-west bend, the tip of the hooked point east of its mouth, the north-west corner of the sea cove beyond. Residuals 10.5, 1.6, 9.4 m. A free similarity fit on the same three points fits them within 5 m but at 0.163 m/px, 15% larger than the survey: the surface features and the cave don't share one scale. The airspace then lands by the big white tent and round palapa north-west of La Isla, where no open water shows any more. Compared with the unverified Beddows 2003 sketch (x-caret.json): its injection-site - A - caleta passage runs 10-30 m east of this map's main passage, with A about 75 m south-south-west of cenote de Felipe; both are guesses on park landmarks. No OSM check: Overpass (mail.ru, overpass-api.de, kumi) timed out.",
