  "symbols": {
    "why": "Overlined numbers are floor depths in metres (the map's own note). OCR found 8 of the 10; the two 8s on the east branch are added by hand. The plain (not overlined) numbers 2, 1, 3, 2 beside the passages have no legend: not kept (ceiling heights? see report). 'p. N m to Xcaret airspace' and cenote de Felipe's '53 m to Xcaret airspace' are penetrations from the open water of the Xcaret airspace; the 4 metre pit is a pit depth; 'passage blocked by boulders' at the north passage's end is the impassable end. Twelve wavy water-flow arrows, all pointing downstream towards the Xcaret airspace and on to cenote de los franceses and the sea, except one in the airspace pointing north-east (bearings from the map's up). No letter codes, no bones (none drawn or written).",
